{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Let death</b> — Rabbi Moses said: the meaning is יָשִׁי מָוֶת (let death come upon them). And the meaning of יָשִׁי — that death would be a creditor to them, that it would take their souls. And others said: [it is] from the root of נְשַׁנְיִי, that Elohim causes them to forget death and not bring it to mind, until they descend alive to Sheol. If so, the form of יָשִׁי would be like the pattern of אַל־תִּמְחִי צוּר יְלָדְךָ תָּשִׁי, where the word is milraʿ. And some say: that it is missing alef, from הֵשִׁיאַנִי, and it is close [in meaning]. And the meaning: He deceives them so that they do not notice and descend alive to Sheol. Rabbi Moses said: בִּמְגוֹרָם בְּחַבּוּרָתָם, like הֲע֣וֹד הַזֶּ֓רַע בַּמְּגוֹרָה. And what seems correct to me: in the land of their sojourn, corresponding to בָּעִיר."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:55.315465754Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}